{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-041",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 41,
  "title": "Job 41",
  "display_title": "Job 41",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 41,
  "sortOrder": 18041,
  "verseCount": 34,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook? or his tongue with a cord which thou lettest down?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Canst thou put an hook into his nose? or bore his jaw through with a thorn?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Will he make many supplications unto thee? will he speak soft words unto thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Will he make a covenant with thee? wilt thou take him for a servant for ever?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Wilt thou play with him as with a bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy maidens?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Shall the companions make a banquet of him? shall they part him among the merchants?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Canst thou fill his skin with barbed irons? or his head with fish spears?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Lay thine hand upon him, remember the battle, do no more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Behold, the hope of him is in vain: shall not one be cast down even at the sight of him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "None is so fierce that dare stir him up: who then is able to stand before me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Who hath prevented me, that I should repay him? whatsoever is under the whole heaven is mine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "I will not conceal his parts, nor his power, nor his comely proportion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Who can discover the face of his garment? or who can come to him with his double bridle?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth are terrible round about.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "His scales are his pride, shut up together as with a close seal.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "By his neesings a light doth shine, and his eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Out of his mouth go burning lamps, and sparks of fire leap out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as out of a seething pot or caldron.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth out of his mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "In his neck remaineth strength, and sorrow is turned into joy before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm in themselves; they cannot be moved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, as hard as a piece of the nether millstone.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "When he raiseth up himself, the mighty are afraid: by reason of breakings they purify themselves.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "The sword of him that layeth at him cannot hold: the spear, the dart, nor the habergeon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "He esteemeth iron as straw, and brass as rotten wood.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Darts are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the shaking of a spear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Sharp stones are under him: he spreadeth sharp pointed things upon the mire.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of ointment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "He maketh a path to shine after him; one would think the deep to be hoary.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Upon earth there is not his like, who is made without fear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:41:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "He beholdeth all high things: he is a king over all the children of pride.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 41:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:41:34"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
